=== tt new --help
Write the manifest a tt package is described by: the format version, the package
name, the Tarantool and tt version requirements and an empty [dependencies]
table for tt package add to write into. The name comes from -n, or from the
directory when that is already a package name — lowercase letters, digits and
dashes, starting with a letter. Components and products are left as commented
examples, since their contents depend on a layout only the author knows. An
existing app.manifest.toml is never overwritten — the command fails instead.
This is not tt create, which lays out a whole application from a template; tt
new adds one file to a directory that may already hold a project.

