=== tt package install --help
Unpack a package archive into the chosen scope and bring the tree to a runnable
state. A with-deps archive in the project scope is a plain offline extraction;
otherwise the package is unpacked and its dependencies are refetched from the
registry using the lock's pins. Several packages installed into one project
share a .rocks/ tree, so a dependency they lock at different versions is
reconciled to one both accept, or the install fails with an explanation.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt package install ARCHIVE... [flags]

  tt package install ARCHIVE... [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
      --force          reinstall over an existing package (destructive)
  -h, --help           help for install
      --locked         fail if the archive lock does not match its manifest
      --scope string   install scope: project, user or system (default
                       "project")
      --upgrade        install over an existing package only when the archive
                       version is higher
  -y, --yes            skip the confirmation prompt when reconciling shared
                       dependencies
[0;1;39m
GLOBAL FLAGS[0m
  -C, --directory string   work on the project in DIR, as if it were the current
                           directory

=== tt package list --help
Show the packages present in the chosen scope: in the project scope the
project's own package plus every guest installed from an archive. The source is
the metadata install records under .rocks/manifests/, so nothing is fetched and
nothing is resolved. This is what is on disk — not what the current manifest
declares, which is what tt package deps reports. --tree additionally shows each
package's dependencies and, for every one of them, whether another package holds
it too — that is, whether it would be removed along with the package or stay.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt package list [flags]

  tt package list [flags]
[0;1;39m
