=== tt package uninstall --help
Remove a guest package: its files and its metadata, plus every shared dependency
that nothing else still needs. A dependency is owned by every installed package
whose lock pins it, so one that another package still holds stays in place. The
project's own package — the one app.manifest.toml in the working directory
declares — is not a guest, and uninstall refuses to remove it.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt package uninstall NAME [flags]

  tt package uninstall NAME [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
  -h, --help           help for uninstall
      --scope string   scope to remove from: project, user or system (default
                       "project")
  -y, --yes            skip the confirmation prompt
[0;1;39m
GLOBAL FLAGS[0m
  -C, --directory string   work on the project in DIR, as if it were the current
                           directory

=== tt package update --help
Re-resolve app.manifest.lock, taking the newest version every constraint allows.
This is the only command that pulls newer registry versions: a release upstream
never makes a lock stale by itself, so a build keeps the versions it has until
an update is asked for. With NAME only that dependency is freed and every other
version is held, so the diff stays confined to it and whatever its new version
requires. No declaration is changed — app.manifest.toml is not touched at all —
and nothing is fetched into .rocks/.

[0;1;39mUSAGE[0m
  tt package update [NAME] [flags]

  tt package update [NAME] [flags]
[0;1;39m
FLAGS[0m
  -h, --help                   help for update
      --registry stringArray   rock server to use instead of the configured
                               ones: an http(s) URL or a local directory; repeat
                               to give an ordered list (overrides TT_REGISTRIES
                               and [platform].registries)
[0;1;39m
GLOBAL FLAGS[0m
  -C, --directory string   work on the project in DIR, as if it were the current
                           directory

